            r1_brief: `Monday 11 January 2027. You have spent eleven years as head of maintenance at Metalúrgica Mera and on 31 January you leave to advise on your own on maintenance plans and quality audits. On Friday the plant director offered you four days a week at the factory, on his schedule and with his email, for EUR 5,200 a month "as a freelancer". Your friend Paula Rey, a tax adviser, told you: "The legal form is not the first thing; the first thing is whom you invoice, how you set money aside and what you sign." Today you choose how you register, what you answer Mera and how you organise the money.`,
            r2_brief: `Monday 5 April 2027. You have filed your first quarter. Ostsee Anlagenbau, a company in Kiel (Germany), offers you an EUR 12,000 audit and asks how you will invoice the VAT. Your invoices come out of a Word template and the quarter's VAT caught you with a thin account. Today you decide what you invoice with, what you do about the German client and how you file VAT.`,
            r3_brief: `Monday 5 July 2027. Frigoríficos do Orzán wants to hire you for a maintenance plan at its cold-storage plant and sends you its standard contract: unlimited liability and payment at 90 days. A mistake in a plan like that can stop a line: a EUR 400,000 claim is not impossible. And Talleres Sada has owed you an invoice of EUR 9,000 (plus VAT) for 90 days. Today you decide your insurance, what you sign and what you do about the unpaid invoice.`,
